<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyen Van Linh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a>–<a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nguyễn Văn Linh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nguyen Van Linh was general secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam">Communist Party of Vietnam</a> from 1986 to 1991. A veteran of the struggle in the south, he became party leader at the Sixth Party Congress of December 1986, which adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doi-moi">Doi Moi</a> reforms, moving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> from central planning towards a market economy. He also oversaw the withdrawal of Vietnamese troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-van-linh.jpg" alt="Nguyen Van Linh" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CalCoWSpiBudSu · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C3%A1m_L%C3%AA_Thanh_v%C3%A0_Nguy%E1%BB%85n_V%C4%83n_Linh_(cropped)_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
